.\" FreeBASIC NuttX SDK
.\" -------------------
.\" File: nuttx-http-server.1
.\" Purpose: Document the installed temporary NuttX file server.
.\" Responsibilities: Describe the bounded HTTP service used for board transfers.
.\" This file intentionally does not describe general-purpose web hosting.
.\"
.TH NUTTX-HTTP-SERVER 1 "2026-07-30" "FreeBASIC NuttX SDK" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nuttx-http-server \- serve NuttX module files over HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nuttx-http-server
.BI --directory " DIR"
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nuttx-http-server
serves files from one directory for the temporary HTTP transfer used by the
FreeBASIC ESP32-P4 workflow. Requests are restricted to that directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --directory " DIR"
Select the directory to serve.
.TP
.BI --bind " ADDRESS"
Set the listening address. The default is 0.0.0.0.
.TP
.BI --port " PORT"
Set the listening TCP port. The default is 8008.
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbc-nuttx-esp32p4 (1),
.BR nuttx-remote-console (1)
.\"
.\" end of nuttx-http-server.1
